{"title":"1971 AHSME Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For each integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/9/0c9c0479fbd8aad814e20f8d875602b38a115c4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"13\" />, there is a mathematical system in which two or more positive integers are defined \nto be congruent if they leave the same non-negative remainder when divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/4/0b4a6d41204181432504f1108ded79e4a49e0e03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N.$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/e/e7e1eff262feb5ac63c8e44d57403edd6d6a3540.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$69,90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/2/b829a6f0810a25e9ca9f85d690f2bafd0f2c1773.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$125$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> are \ncongruent in one such system, then in that same system, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/e/87edbdda753b32453027dc7cab023c0743b6b243.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$81$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> is congruent to\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/f/92fe280ad199df9774fd62a5a24bab4d2c4340cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }3\\qquad \\textbf{(B) }4\\qquad \\textbf{(C) }5\\qquad \\textbf{(D) }7\\qquad  \\textbf{(E) }8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"353\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The \"mathematical system\" being alluded to is <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Modulo\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Modulo\">modulo</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, so we shall be using such notation for convenience. \nFrom the problem, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/b/cfb3e745e06efe3e41b63b16d50caf7cf4e58d75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$69 \\equiv 90 \\equiv 125 \\mod N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"184\" height=\"14\" />, so the difference between each of these numbers must be a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/c/49c365ef57ba5f701685445facbf68205576d420.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90-69=21=3\\cdot7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"158\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/1/18165a26d92db54d4d6933ac310646514311e6b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$125-90=35=5\\cdot7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"167\" height=\"15\" />. The only common factors between these two numbers are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, but we know from the problem that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/3/b53fcb30eff54ca37056e56453d8f8c71665a16b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N\\neq1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/4/ac4bc1e272354b8a21af83b5df5184ada6612b59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N=7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" />. Now, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/2/362f54167da386e11357d6ceb60b5079c55bf89a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$81 \\equiv 77+4 \\equiv 4 \\mod 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"189\" height=\"16\" />, so our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/9/2494711a9f0508844ca4716f548a3252bc93cc6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME\" title=\"1971 AHSME\">1971 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1971 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1971 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1971\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1971 AHSME Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1971 AHSME Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1971 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1971 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1971 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1971 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1971 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1971 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1971 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1971 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1971 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1971 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1971 AHSME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1971 AHSME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1971 AHSME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971